Explanation of fast PWM: 

It is one of the 2 PWM mods Atmega328P offers, in this mode of PWM, the tcnt0 goes from 0 to 0xFF(or OCR0A, based on the wave generation mode selected), for each cycle, the tcnt0 is compared to OCR0x and the corresponding output compare pin is set to high or low. 

In non inverting mode, the output compare pin (OC0x), when the tcnt0 is at BOTTOM(0x00), a rising edge is triggered and it stays like that till there is a compare match between tcnt0 and the OCR0x, which causes a falling edge, and it stays like that for the rest of the period, that is, from OCR0x -> 255. And when the tcnt0 wraps back down to 0, a rising edge is triggered, making the pin high, and this continues.  So the duty cycle(the time for which a signal is HIGH in a period) for inverting non mode will be: (OCR0x value / 256) * 100.		(256 since we also wrap back around from 255 to 0). 


In inverting mode, the output compare pin sees a falling edge when the tcnt0 is at bottom, and there is a rising edge when there is a compare match between 
OCR0x and TCNT0, basically LOW when the tcnt0 is below OCR0x and HIGH when it is above OCR0x. So the duty cycle for inverting mode is:  
( (256 - OCR0x value) / 256) * 100 


In fast PWM mode, the frequency of the produced signal will be: Clock_frequency / (N * 256), where N is the prescaler.  



Explanation of the code: 

1)The first section of the code is macros definition of the addresses of the registers, which reduces redundancy across the whole program and makes our life easier and makes the code mode hygienic. 

2) The WGM02:00 bits are set to 0-1-1, since I want to use the mode 3, where the timer is in FAST PWM mode with the top as 0xFF and the bottom is 0x00. 

3) I also ensure the timer is enabled by clearing the PRTIM0 bit in the PRR register. 

This step is not really required since arduino already handles it for us, but this is a good practice to have. 

4) The CS02:00 bits are set to 0-1-1, for selecting the 64 prescaler. 

5) The COM0A1:0 bits are set to 10( binary), to set the compare output pin to non inverting mode. 













